WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.150
If a washing machine robot or retirement lottery
winners sound like can't-miss material, then

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.580
check out these 2022 movie dramas that flew
under the radar.

00:00:08.966 --> 00:00:13.759
Steve Pink might not be the biggest name in
showbiz, but he did direct the cult classic

00:00:13.759 --> 00:00:16.650
comedies Accepted and Hot Tub Time Machine.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:21.790
It turns out he also has a knack for drama,
based on the candid and touching The Wheel,

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.570
which is about a young couple on the verge
of divorce.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:28.300
Albee and Walker met when they were 12 and
fell for each other hard.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:33.044
As The Wheel begins, their eight-year-long
marriage is dangerously close to complete collapse.

00:00:33.044 --> 00:00:37.579
So they rent an Airbnb cabin from a lovely
couple in the woods to give their union one

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:38.870
last shot.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:43.270
With the guide of a dime-a-dozen self-help
book, Walker wants Albee to go through a set

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.090
of questions over the weekend.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:49.570
But she isn't exactly keen on participating,
as she's really just waiting for the perfect

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.750
moment to end their relationship.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:55.879
During all this, the owners of the cabin begin
to interfere with their guests' marital issues,

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:57.550
which only makes matters worse.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:01.600
What makes The Wheel worthy of praise are
the central performances by Amber Midthunder

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:07.323
and Taylor Gray, whose chemistry is palpable
as their characters' opposite personalities clash.

00:01:07.323 --> 00:01:11.540
The result is a heartbreakingly honest drama
where we get hurt just as much as they do

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.409
by the time the credits start to roll.

00:01:13.894 --> 00:01:19.566
A veteran of several Ricky Gervais projects,
David Earl is a familiar face to fans of British comedy.

00:01:19.566 --> 00:01:25.130
He usually plays shy, introverted, and often
miserable outcasts who are inherently funny

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.920
and relatable by design.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.220
In the Jim Archer-directed feature Brian and
Charles, Earl delivers another variation of

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:33.830
his typically quirky and pathetic persona.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:38.390
The film follows Earl as a lonely man named
Brian, who lives by himself in a village in

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:39.680
the Welsh countryside.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.000
He spends most of his days scavenging scrap
and using whatever he can find to build odd

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.070
things that nobody really needs.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:50.430
One day, he stumbles upon a mannequin's head
along with an old, broken washing machine,

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.820
which leads to him building a robot.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.700
The thing doesn't work at first, but after
a stormy night, the robot mysteriously comes

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.430
alive and learns to communicate, and Brian
names him Charles.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:04.450
What follows is a weird but sweet friendship
between an amusing machine and an isolated

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:08.700
man who longed for a companion his whole life
but never had one, until now.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.890
Brian and Charles' humor is delightfully strange
and awkward, but its most endearing aspect

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:17.358
is how it depicts a touching benevolence underneath
its protagonist's trauma.

00:02:17.358 --> 00:02:18.475
"You soppy sod.

00:02:19.386 --> 00:02:20.799
Look, he wants a kiss."

00:02:20.799 --> 00:02:21.299
"Ooh."

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:25.762
"Right."

00:02:26.144 --> 00:02:30.784
It's a little surprising that a neo-western
like Montana Story didn't appeal to a larger audience.

00:02:30.784 --> 00:02:35.700
Despite generally positive reviews, this tragic
and untamed American family drama featuring

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.600
Haley Lu Richardson and Owen Teague remains
a hidden gem.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.190
Perhaps that's because its emotionally raw
story doesn't go easy on the heart.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:47.720
Erin, played by Richardson, and Cal, played
by Teague, are two estranged siblings who

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.700
went their separate ways after a rough and
abusive childhood.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:55.430
Now, after many years, Erin returns to the
ranch that she abandoned to escape her violent,

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:56.450
alcoholic father.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:00.409
While she ran away, Cal stayed behind, and
now he's the one who looks after their dying

00:03:00.409 --> 00:03:03.030
dad and takes care of everything around the
ranch.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.349
Erin only comes back to say goodbye, but she
ends up staying longer than she expected.

00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:11.400
During that time, she and Cal confront their
past and the demons that still haunt them.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:15.010
Now they're both ready to confess their mistakes
and the regrets they buried deep in their

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.260
hearts long ago.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:21.000
Montana Story can be challenging at times,
but if you can endure its bitter emotional

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.940
dynamics, it's a rewarding watch.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:27.090
It seems that every time Zac Efron tries to
show off his acting skills in a role that

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:31.920
demands more from him than being handsome
and charming, the stars just never quite align.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.129
But maybe we should give him more credit,
and the survival drama Gold is just the latest

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:37.519
reason why.

00:03:37.519 --> 00:03:41.430
Director Anthony Hayes's dystopian vision
is a one-man show for the most part.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:45.500
Virgil, played by Efron, is a traveler in
the near future who pays a local man named

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.890
Keith, played by Hayes, to transport him into
an area called The Compound.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:53.290
On their way, they discover a large gold nugget
in the desert stuck underground.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.590
They decide to take it with them, but no matter
how hard they try, it just won't budge.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:01.610
So Keith convinces Virgil to stay behind and
guard their newly found treasure until he

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.780
gets back with the right equipment to dig
it out.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:07.890
What follows are several days in the desert
filled with unbearable heat, scavengers, and

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.280
local predators.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:12.740
Virgil's mental state begins to crack, and
it becomes doubtful whether he can make it

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.239
until his partner returns.

00:04:14.239 --> 00:04:19.223
Efron delivers a powerful performance as his
character slowly breaks down physically and mentally.

00:04:19.223 --> 00:04:22.124
You feel his suffering and root for him with
all your heart.

00:04:22.124 --> 00:04:26.400
Despite the unbalanced pacing and flawed script,
Efron's effort comes through, making Gold

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.773
an underrated gem that's worth a watch.

00:04:28.773 --> 00:04:29.576
"Take it easy.

00:04:29.576 --> 00:04:30.576
Breathe.

00:04:32.081 --> 00:04:32.944
That's it."

00:04:33.152 --> 00:04:37.460
Jerry and Marge Go Large is one of the most
charmingly delightful dramedies of the year.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.210
It's low-key yet exciting, funny, and even
moving.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.350
It's an unbelievable story told in an unfussy
way.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:47.160
That lack of heightened drama might be why
it never took off, but the moderate pacing

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.750
combined with restrained performances from
veterans Bryan Cranston and Annette Bening

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.120
fit the tone and script perfectly.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.990
Jerry and Marge are a long-married couple
who have just entered retirement.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:01.850
Workaholic Jerry simply doesn't know what
to do with all the newfound free time he suddenly

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:05.070
has after working for the same company 42
years.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.250
But then he finds a loophole in a lottery
game called WinFall.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:12.090
To find out whether his theory works in practice,
he buys a lot of tickets.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:15.440
He ends up winning, but he's afraid to tell
his wife, since they don't have much money

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.130
saved for their golden years.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:21.630
But when Marge finds out accidentally, she
sees an opportunity to spice up their marriage.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:26.290
So she joins him on a journey that ends up
bringing them a lot of cash and a shot not

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:30.060
just at changing their lives but also the
town they love wholeheartedly.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:34.160
Jerry and Marge got so-so reviews, and that
might be the most common opinion from general

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.600
audiences as well.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.410
It's hard not to like this lovely little gem,
even if it can't give you everything to fall

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:40.922
in love with it on a first watch.

00:05:40.922 --> 00:05:42.352
"Oh, uh, please.

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:44.343
'Jerry and Marge' is fine."

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:48.949
As They Made Us, Mayim Bialik's directorial
debut, features a set of great actors and

00:05:48.949 --> 00:05:53.259
a delicate portrayal of a Jewish family spending
their last days with their dying father while

00:05:53.259 --> 00:05:56.539
his physical and mental health rapidly deteriorates.

00:05:56.539 --> 00:06:00.790
Dianna Agron plays Abigail, the daughter,
caretaker, and glue of the family.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:04.560
She's also a single mother raising two kids
while trying to take care of her elderly father

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.520
Eugene, played by Dustin Hoffman.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:10.680
She has an awful lot on her plate, and her
mother is more of an obstacle than a helper.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:15.150
Abigail genuinely cares about her dad, despite
the rough and traumatic upbringing he put

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:16.970
her and her brother through.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:20.590
When death comes scarily close for Eugene,
Abigail gives it one last shot to convince

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:23.870
her brother to say goodbye to their father,
while he still can.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:27.449
As They Made Us slowly works its way through
your heart and crushes it.

00:06:27.449 --> 00:06:31.939
Hoffman gives a performance for the ages,
while everyone else around him is just as solid.

00:06:31.939 --> 00:06:36.319
There aren't any big surprises in this drama,
but it's so well-written and acted that it

00:06:36.319 --> 00:06:37.590
doesn't need them.

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:40.220
"I didn't necessarily want to Write it.

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:43.107
I felt a need to write some of these
things down."

00:06:43.107 --> 00:06:47.940
After putting in the hard work as a supporting
actor for three decades, Clifton Collins Jr.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.400
proved more than capable to carry an entire
film on his shoulders.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:56.210
Jockey is a fantastic, soulful movie that
doesn't only do justice to Collins, but also

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:59.569
to a sport that's been mistreated so many
times on screen before.

00:06:59.569 --> 00:07:03.070
Collins plays Jackson Silva, who's been a
jockey his whole life.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:07.060
Horse racing is in his blood, and despite
the several serious injuries he's suffered

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:09.740
during his career, he doesn't want to retire.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:13.680
After all, he isn't really good at anything
else, and he knows horses better than people.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.900
But he can't reverse time and what it's done
to his body.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:18.340
That doesn't mean he won't try, though.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:22.060
With the help of a skillful trainer named
Ruth, he decides to take part in the upcoming

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:26.620
championship that will most likely be his
last, if he can finish it at all.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:31.340
What he can't be prepared for, though, is
the racing newcomer who claims to be his son.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:36.501
Jockey is a superb drama with a sublime atmosphere
that not only does right by the world of horse

00:07:36.501 --> 00:07:39.710
racing, but gives us a chance to feel like
we're a part of it.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:44.530
In a perfect world, The Survivor wouldn't
have been a TV film produced by HBO but instead

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:49.130
a big-budget studio flick that would earn
Ben Foster his first Oscar nomination.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:53.560
But in reality, this biopic about Holocaust
survivor Harry Haft is a drama that flew under

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.520
the radar, even though critics praised it
upon its release.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:00.900
The plot follows Haft post-World War II on
his road to becoming a professional boxer

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:05.220
after surviving the concentration camps by
fighting his fellow inmates to death.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:09.690
Besides making a living, his goal is to gain
enough publicity to find his long-lost love,

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.770
who was separated from him during the war.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:16.370
As he continuously grapples with his past
trauma, we see flashbacks of him in the camps,

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:17.870
depicting how he stayed alive.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:22.150
Though The Survivor is a little uneven as
it ambitiously attempts to cover several decades

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:26.479
of Haft's tumultuous life, Foster's exceptional
performance is what pulls it together.

00:08:26.479 --> 00:08:30.520
He's a little too old to play Haft in his
younger years, but it doesn't feel that way.

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:35.320
He convincingly conveys all the anger and
terror he went through in horrifying experiences

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.130
that left him with survivor's guilt.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:39.805
"You murdered your own people."

00:08:42.579 --> 00:08:44.276
"Why like this?"

00:08:44.811 --> 00:08:49.520
One Moment is perhaps most notable as the
final film for legendary character actor Danny

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:53.230
Aiello , who passed away in 2019 after a brief
illness.

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:56.550
His performance as Joe McGuinness couldn't
have been more fitting.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:09:00.279
As a recently widowed husband, Joe tries to
cope with the loss of his wife by becoming

00:09:00.279 --> 00:09:03.399
more present in his middle-aged children's
lives.

00:09:03.399 --> 00:09:07.000
The plot follows the three McGuinness siblings
and how they operate their overwhelmingly

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.209
busy lives.

00:09:08.209 --> 00:09:12.410
Besides working and raising kids, they're
also trying to comfort their ailing father,

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:15.930
who struggles with increasing physical and
mental health issues.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:20.149
It provides an excellent opportunity for Aiello
to showcase his subtle and charming skills

00:09:20.149 --> 00:09:21.710
one last time.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:25.589
Even at the age of 86, Aiello delivers the
kind of performance that made him one of the

00:09:25.589 --> 00:09:29.930
most memorable character actors around during
an almost 50-year-long career.

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:33.680
The rest of the cast does a good job, but
none of them can quite rise to Aiello's level

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.500
as an experienced veteran.

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:38.267
He's the heart of the movie and the one who
makes it all work.

00:09:38.396 --> 00:09:43.570
Comedian Jerrod Carmichael's feature directorial
debut, On The Count of Three is a dramedy

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:48.140
exploring mental health and trauma with pitch-black
humor and a raw emotional palette.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:52.170
The plot follows Carmichael and Christopher
Abbott as Val and Kevin, two best friends

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.440
at the end of their ropes.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.480
Val is depressed, dreading life at his mundane
day job.

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:00.410
After receiving a promotion, he walks to the
bathroom and tries to hang himself but gets

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:01.410
interrupted.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:05.600
Meanwhile, Kevin is in a psychiatric hospital
after a suicide attempt, trying to convince

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.980
a social worker that he doesn't have suicidal
thoughts anymore.

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:13.450
When Val shows up to Kevin and asks him to
run away together, Kevin doesn't hesitate.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:16.910
Once they flee, Val suggests they should help
kill each other.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:21.050
He's thought of everything: two handguns in
a backpack, an abandoned parking lot behind

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:25.030
a strip club, and an unchangeable determination
to go through with it.

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:28.480
On the Count of Three tackles mental health
issues without illusions.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:32.600
It's a poignant and realistic depiction of
people experiencing suicidal thoughts with

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:33.924
grace and empathy.

